  "slug": "dynamics-long-4a04",
  "summary": "Preprints track how long-range and multipartite entanglement persist under decoherence, Floquet driving and quenches, and shape late-time observables.",
  "synthesis": "The main thread is the use of time evolution to reveal nonlocal quantum structure that local or static probes miss. A decoherence-driven transition from a 1D SPT state to a trivial product state carries hidden long-range correlations. Floquet drives that proliferate fermionic anyons in the toric code leave a long-time state with long-range entanglement, presented as a Floquet analog of mixed-state topological order. In crosscap states, local symmetry breaking grows while entanglement decreases, because the asymmetry is initially encoded in long-range entanglement. Crystal quenches in a tight-binding chain show configurations with no irreducible tripartite entanglement. Charged dual-unitary circuits with a symmetry-breaking impurity display non-monotonic entropy growth. Open-system work extracts a non-Hermitian Lindbladian invariant from covariance-matrix relaxation and links graph spectra to late-time qubit concurrence. Two complementary studies connect chaos onset in spin ladders, and the QMC sign problem, to entanglement and nonstabilizerness.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
